>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (These constructs arise from the direct observation of seemingly directly opposite phenomena: the cycles of day and night, mathematical duality in operations or , more recently, the wave-particle duality. All of these show that duality is more than a mere human-made concept: it is a recurring mechanisms that is present across dozens of knowledge fields. But why? )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (Duality beats the limits of a single-perspective framework of our world: by using a lens of dicotomy, it enables us to look past a single description, it creates links between concepts and makes them complimentary rather than contradictory. In doing so, it makes us be just a bit closer to the true richness of the universe.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (Here we explore some of the roles this concept plays, helping us understand how our world works and the intricacies it entails - from the relationship between philosophy and maths, through psychossomatic open questions and the dicotomy between classical and quantum physics - we will explore some of the biggest contrasts in science an try to make sense of the duality that reigns our world.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
