/P 360 0 R
/E (The Measurement Problem)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
508 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 360 0 R
/E (The measurement problem explicitly relates to this crisis between classical physics and quantum mechanics. When a quantum system is observed or measured, it has a single, definite outcome, but prior to observation it existed as a mixture of multiple possible states \(superposition\). Quantum superposition is when a system can have this characteristic of existing in multiple states, behaving like a wave of distinct probabilities. Mathematically, quantum mechanics can predict the odds of where a particle may appear incredibly accurately, but it cannot explain the physical mechanism of this sudden transition. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
