/E (  The monoamine theory wasn't wrong in its approach when it gave us safe, effective medications that have helped millions. But it oversimplified depression into a chemical imbalance that could be fixed with one simple medication. This allowed pharmaceutical marketing to dominate the conversation and left little room for other explanations.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
