/E (  Quantum computers are able to approach certain problems in fundamentally different ways by exploiting the physical laws that govern matter at extremely small scales. Rather than simply making calculations faster, they use quantum phenomena to represent and manipulate information in ways that classical computers cannot efficiently reproduce.)
