/E (   However, technological development rapidly approached the Gen X in the 1990s. Compared to the traditional methods of observation, sophisticated imaging technologies such as X-rays, CTs and MRIs paved the way for evidence-based diagnosis. These tools assisted physicians in making crucial medical decisions. Along with the advancements of medical tools, early paper medical records became digitized, retrieving and storing historical records in an electronic system. This helped doctors compare and interpret data from past diagnoses.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [1]
