/Title (Another important application of pH in pharmaceuticals is understanding protein crystallization, as various pH levels can affect the structure and solubility of proteins. Investigations focused on human insulin found that higher pH levels increased its solubility, an important property that ensures it can move into the blood quickly to manage blood sugar levels. This holds significance when it comes to the use of insulin as a treatment for diabetics, as while short-acting insulin must be soluble so it can be taken quickly before meals to prevent blood glucose levels being too high when carbohydrates are eaten, long-acting insulin should not be as soluble so it can work slowly to keep levels stable between meals, meaning it is important that pharmacologists understand the nuance between the pH values of different forms of insulin.)
