/Title (Quantum states behave somewhat like waves, as they can reinforce or cancel one another through a process called quantum interference. You might think of this like an artist working on a drawing, strengthening certain lines while erasing others until the intended image becomes clearer. Similarly, quantum algorithms manipulate interfering states so that pathways leading towards useful answers are strengthened, while others are suppressed. When the qubits are finally measured, the desired result is therefore more likely to emerge. Quantum algorithms that feature this mathematical manipulation to reveal useful structures and hidden correlations are extremely powerful for certain tasks.)
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3422 0 R
/Next 3428 0 R
>>
endobj
