3443 0 obj
<<
/Title (When actually pairing the natural numbers with the integers, it is best to arrange them in such a way that every odd number in the natural numbers is paired with a positive number in the integers, and every even number in the natural numbers is paired with a negative number in the integers. If we count both the set of even natural numbers and the set of odd natural numbers separately, it is clear that both of these are infinite sets. Therefore, the natural numbers can pair with the integers infinitely in both the positive and negative directions. As every natural number appears exactly once, and every integer also appears exactly once, we have constructed a bijection between the two sets, proving they have the same cardinality.)
/Dest [54 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3445 0 R
/Next 3441 0 R
>>
endobj
